  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nEcuador\nEcuador*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nEcuador\nVisa regime\nCitizens of the Republic of Ecuador can apply for a Montenegrin visa at the Embassy of Montenegro in the Republic of Argentina in Buenos Aires.\nDiplomatic relations\nThe Republic of Ecuador recognized Montenegro on 26 September 2009. Diplomatic relations between Montenegro and the Republic of Ecuador were established on the same day (Foreign Ministers Milan Rocen and Fander Falconi Benitez signed the Protocol on the Establishment of Diplomatic Relations, on the sidelines of the 64th session of the UN General Assembly).\nEcuador covers Montenegro on a non-resident basis, from the Embassy in Rome. Ambassador Nelson Francisco Robelly Lozada received the agreement on June 3, 2019.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
